mary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.75,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":[],"finding":"The plan's core premise — that after A4-2, branch 3 (`_compute_mutations_emit_both`) emits `(outbound, update)` mutations with an EMPTY effective field payload — is not backed by the committed code and rests on an unverifiable prerequisite (A4-2). The committed `_compute_mutations_emit_both` already gates its emit behind `if changed:` (an empty resolved payload emits NOTHING today), and for a key-set previous snapshot (`local_fields = {}`) it resolves `changed` to `{field: None, ...}` over every non-excluded Jira field — a NON-empty payload — because `changed` is built over `set(local_fields) | set(jira_fields)` and `local_val != jira_val` holds for each. So against the committed snapshot there is no empty-payload branch-3 emit to short-circuit; the described behavior depends wholly on A4-2's uncommitted changes, which cannot be confirmed.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdf143bfbd280b41c","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Context / Approach — 'can enter branch 3 with empty local fields'; 'Short-circuit the branch-3 emit ... when the resolved effective field payload is empty'","norm_id":"n5b1d208cd3533790","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","scenarios":[],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3333,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":[],"finding":"The gate condition 'when the resolved effective field payload is empty' is ambiguous and risks a wrong implementation: for a key-set previous snapshot the branch-3 `changed` dict is NOT empty (it is populated with every jira field mapped to local_val=None), and the existing `if changed:` gate already emits. The payload is only empty AFTER `_mutation_to_batch_dict` resolves a bare (non-`changed_fields`) update payload to `{}`. A naive `if not changed` short-circuit would never fire for the key-set case and would silently fail AC-1.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1e1c08d7a8a83f77","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section: 'Short-circuit the branch-3 emit in compute_mutations when the resolved effective field payload is empty.'","norm_id":"n5f9f94c358d12551","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","scenarios":[],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Restate the gate in terms the differ can evaluate without the applier, e.g.: 'Short-circuit the branch-3 (outbound, update) emit when `local_fields` is empty for that key (so every entry in `changed` is a spurious None-diff against the key-set membership marker), which is exactly the case whose bare payload the applier later resolves to {} fields.' Ensu